    "created_at": "2019-12-18T14:25:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-12-18T14:25:06Z",
    "body": "Assuming that the HTTPS resource sends either `Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-site;` or `Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-site;`, it can't be loaded by an HTTP context (as no HTTP context will be match either of those declarations (see step 5 of the existing https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#cross-origin-resource-policy-check and the note in step 7 of https://mikewest.github.io/corpp/#abstract-opdef-cross-origin-resource-policy-check).\r\n\r\nIf the response sets `CORP: cross-site`, then you're right, but it's a resource that's explicitly not restricted. That seems less risky (and wouldn't be prevented by enabling COEP for non-secure contexts).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/567053038/reactions",
